      "notes": "CG envelope forward-limit taper corrected to TCDS 2A13 Item XIV Normal Category: (+83.0) to (+93.0) at 1950 lb or less; (+87.0) to (+93.0) at 2325 lb (straight-line variation). Module was a near-flat forward limit 82.0 rising only to 83.0 at 2325 lb -> up to 4.0 in MORE nose-heavy-permissive than certified at gross (FD-413 forward-limit-taper defect). Aft limit 93.0 was already correct. front_seats_arm 85.5 -> 80.5: TCDS Item XIV 'No. of Seats Normal Category: 4 (2 at +80.5, 2 at +118.1)' — the Warrior/stretched-Cherokee front-seat arm is +80.5, not the short-body 140/235 +85.5; rear_seats_arm 118.1, baggage_arm 142.8 (200 lb at +142.8), fuel_arm 95.0 (50 gal at +95) confirmed CORRECT against TCDS Item XIV. Utility Category envelope (2 seats, 1950 lb) not modeled. DEFERRED (Track B, fingerprint/drift-coupled): empty_weight/empty_weight_arm nominal placeholders (TCDS Empty Weight C.G. Range: None); usable_fuel_gal 48 vs TCDS 50 gal total. Full findings: docs/fd-419-s2-piper-singles-wb-findings-2026-07-26.md."
